# .github/actions/harden-checkout carries the Harden runner + checkout
# security config (egress-policy, persist-credentials) for all 25 gate
# workflows in this repository (issue #813). A change here affects every
# gate at once, so it requires the repo owner's review.
#
# Note: this file alone does not enforce review -- it only takes effect once
# branch protection's "Require review from Code Owners" is enabled, which is
# a GitHub Settings change outside this repo's tracked files.
/.github/actions/harden-checkout/ @tvna

# .github/trusted-bots.yml grants an identity-based exemption from the
# independent-review-pending merge gate (issue #1858) -- an unreviewed
# edit could silently widen who bypasses independent review.
/.github/trusted-bots.yml @tvna

# .github/rulesets/main.json's commit_author_email_pattern/
# committer_email_pattern rules are the second trust anchor
# head_commit_identity_matches_bot() depends on (issue #1858) -- an
# unreviewed edit to either pattern could loosen it enough for an
# arbitrary commit email to pass, the same class of risk trusted-bots.yml
# above is already protected against.
/.github/rulesets/main.json @tvna
